From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 18:53:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 105/105] v4l2videodec: Return success from a complete drain

The processing thread ends a drain with GST_V4L2_FLOW_LAST_BUFFER, a
custom success value, and finish() returned it as is. At the end of the
stream the base class only posts "No valid frames decoded before end of
stream" when the drain returned GST_FLOW_OK, so that check never ran for
this element: a stream of which the device decoded no frame, e.g. one
the driver refuses, ended with EOS and no error.

Return GST_FLOW_OK for a complete drain.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 sys/v4l2/gstv4l2videodec.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sys/v4l2/gstv4l2videodec.c b/sys/v4l2/gstv4l2videodec.c
index d65d75f..1e7c1a5 100644
--- a/sys/v4l2/gstv4l2videodec.c
+++ b/sys/v4l2/gstv4l2videodec.c
@@ -710,6 +710,12 @@ gst_v4l2_video_dec_finish (GstVideoDecoder * decoder)
   if (ret == GST_FLOW_FLUSHING)
     ret = self->output_flow;
 
+  /* The processing thread ends a complete drain with the last buffer: that
+   * is success. The base class only checks at the end of the stream that
+   * something was decoded when the drain returns GST_FLOW_OK. */
+  if (ret == GST_V4L2_FLOW_LAST_BUFFER)
+    ret = GST_FLOW_OK;
+
   GST_DEBUG_OBJECT (decoder, "Done draining buffers");
 
   /* Draining of the capture buffer has completed.
